<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bay of Pigs invasion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1961">1961</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bay of Pigs invasion was a failed landing in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> on 17–20 April 1961 by about 1,400 Cuban exiles trained and funded by the CIA, aiming to overthrow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro">Fidel Castro</a>. Without the hoped-for uprising or US air cover, they were defeated within three days and most were captured. The fiasco strengthened Castro, pushed Cuba closer to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and preceded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuban-missile-crisis">Cuban Missile Crisis</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bay-of-pigs-invasion.jpg" alt="Bay of Pigs invasion" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rumlin · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Attack_near_Playa_Giron._April_19,_1961._-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
